      {
        "sequence_id": 1,
        "text": "E. VERBS\n\nTwo verbs occur in Unit 3 which are similar to the four irregular verbs dürfen, können, müssen and wollen already encountered. They are sollen ('to be supposed to') and wissen ('to know (a fact)'). These six verbs occur very frequently in German, and together with one other verb (mögen), occurring very infrequently in the present, make up the complete list of verbs following this particular irregular pattern. For reference purposes all seven verbs are reproduced below in a table showing the ich-form, er-form and wir-form: darf – er darf – dürfen; kann – er kann – können; mag – er mag – mögen; muss – er muss – müssen; soll – er soll – sollen; will – er will – wollen; weiss – er weiss – wissen.\n\nThe lesson notes that there are two other new irregular verbs in this unit, illustrated by the forms halte – hält – halten and behalte – behält – behalten."
      }
